  "updated_at": "2026-07-30T14:48:31.719Z",
  "published_at": "2026-07-30T14:48:31.706Z",
  "id": 203707644505635,
  "uuid": "089dc66d-455f-4f61-bca6-b37a395a8dcb",
  "is_folder": false,
  "content": {
    "_uid": "9001f35d-e9e9-6571-185e-6bf07c3bc291",
    "body": [
      {
        "_uid": "58bf4998-98c7-7b59-9138-e2367e47e5db",
        "content": {
          "type": "doc",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "The announcement was made on Independence Day, August 14, and the award was presented to Dr Abbas in an investiture ceremony on Pakistan Day, 23 March 2016.",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Dr Abbas has been awarded the G.B. Ong Gold Medal from Royal College of Surgeons of Edinburgh in 1992-3, the International Guest Scholarship from American College of Surgeons in 2002, the Tamgha-e-Imtiaz by the President of Pakistan in 2010, and elected a Fellow of the Pakistan Academy of Sciences in 2012.",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "\"This is indeed a huge honour and privilege for my family and me. In essence, it is a joint recognition of my colleagues at the Aga Khan University, for what we do together, and of my family, for their superb support and encouragement,\" said Dr Abbas.",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Dr Abbas holds an MBBS and FCPS from Pakistan, and an FRCS from the Royal Colleges of Surgeons of Edinburgh and Glasgow. He is also a Fellow of the European Board of Urology and the American College of Surgeons. ",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Dr Abbas joined AKU in 1985 as a Resident in the Department of Surgery and is currently a Professor of Urology. He has served in several leadership positions in the University including that of Associate Dean, Postgraduate Medical Education; Medical Director; Associate Dean, Clinical Affairs; Chief Operating Officer, Aga Khan University Hospital, Karachi; and Interim Dean, Medical College before taking up his current role as Dean, Medical College.",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
